# RTK (Rust Token Killer) Automation

Always prefix terminal and CLI execution commands with \tk\ (e.g. \tk git status\, \tk cargo test\, \tk npm test\, \tk pytest\, \tk vitest\, \tk ls\, \tk rg\).
- Output is compressed to save tokens while preserving critical errors and signal.
- In multi-command chains, prefix each sub-command: \tk git add . && rtk git commit -m "update"\.
- Use \tk gain\ to review token savings metrics.
